<p>The most useful Stonly alternatives depend on what you want to replace. Start with Zingtree for connected agent workflows, Knowmax for contact-centre knowledge and guided flows, or ScreenSteps for employee procedures and training. Document360 combines documentation with decision trees, but its documented beta restrictions matter. UserGuiding suits in-product onboarding, while Intercom Fin Procedures offers conversational automation rather than the same click-through guide experience. Keep Stonly if its branching guides and delivery fit your support process. Compare author seats, guide views, active users and AI outcomes separately before deciding which offer is affordable.</p>
<h2>What kind of Stonly replacement do you need?</h2>
<p>A branching troubleshooting guide, an internal procedure, a product tour and an AI conversation can all help someone complete a task. They impose different authoring, maintenance and billing requirements. Treating them as interchangeable creates a shortlist that looks broad but answers the wrong question.</p>
<p>This research-based comparison checks six relevant products against those jobs. Official pages were reviewed on October 14, 2026; no hands-on product benchmark or ticket-deflection measurement was performed. The comparison order follows workflow fit, rather than an unverified overall ranking.</p>
